From 00778d6f86eebd00761a9e812ceb7b3901ad47be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:45:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Client statement: count each receipt once; applied credit
 is not new money

The statement credited a receipt's full amount on every transactions row
linked to it, so applying 300 of credit from a 1,300 receipt put 1,300
on the statement again (a client owing 0 showed 1,300). It also never
credited 7% VAT withheld, crashed on "other payments" receipts, showed
credit balances as debts (abs), and left advances with no invoice off.

- New ClientStatement service builds the statement from invoices,
  receipts (once each: money + WHT/VAT/deduction lines) and credit
  applications (information only). Signed balance with "CR", date range
  with opening balance, open invoices with days overdue, unused credit,
  and a self-check against the per-invoice position.
- Statement page rebuilt (print, Excel, no re-sorting); client page
  summary uses the same figures.
- Analysis and proposal in docs/receipts-and-payments.md section 7.

Tests: 50 passing on SQLite and MariaDB 10.11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
